      "questionText": "Define Skill Gap Analysis and construct a structured Personal Development Plan (PDP) framework for an undergraduate agricultural student aiming for a career in precision agriculture.",
      "contextScenario": "A career mentoring seminar for third-year B.Sc. Agriculture undergraduates.",
      "modelAnswer": "A Skill Gap Analysis is a strategic diagnostic self-assessment wherein an individual systematically compares their current skills, knowledge proficiencies, and experiential competencies against the explicit competency benchmarks demanded by target industry employers or advanced academic programs.\n\nStructured Personal Development Plan (PDP) Framework for Precision Agriculture:\n\n1. Target Career Competency Profiling:\nIdentify the core technical requirements for a Precision Agronomist:\n- Geospatial Analysis (QGIS, satellite imagery processing, NDVI interpretation).\n- Agronomic Diagnostics (soil fertility mapping, Variable Rate fertilization).\n- Data Science Basics (R or Python for agronomic data modeling).\n- Modern Mechanization (drone piloting, GNSS/RTK autosteer systems).\n\n2. Baseline Self-Assessment (Audit):\n- Strengths: Solid grounding in soil chemistry, crop physiology, and entomology from BSc core courses.\n- Identified Gaps: Zero formal experience in GIS software, lack of coding literacy, and no exposure to commercial drone mission planning.\n\n3. Actionable Remediation Pathway (12-Month Timeline):\n- Months 1-3: Complete an introductory MOOC on 'Geographic Information Systems (GIS) in Agriculture' on Coursera or SWAYAM; build 3 sample soil fertility maps in QGIS.\n- Months 4-6: Complete an applied Python/R data science MOOC focusing on agricultural analytics; publish reproducible scripts on GitHub.\n- Months 7-9: Enroll in a DGCA-certified Remote Pilot Training Organization (RPTO) to secure a commercial Remote Pilot Certificate (RPC).\n- Months 10-12: Implement an on-farm field trial during RAWE using drone multispectral imagery and write an evidence-based portfolio project.\n\n4. Evaluation and Review:\nQuarterly reviews tracking portfolio completion, GitHub commits, and mock technical interview performance against industry job listings.",
