      "modelAnswer": "India has pioneered robust national digital learning repositories that eliminate geographical, financial, and institutional barriers to premier agricultural education.\n\n1. SWAYAM PRABHA (Reaching the Unconnected via Satellite DTH):\n- Transmits high-definition educational video lectures 24/7 across 40 dedicated Direct-to-Home (DTH) channels using the GSAT-15 satellite, coordinated technically by BISAG-N Gandhinagar.\n- By broadcasting directly to television sets via free DD Free Dish decoders, it delivers curriculum-mapped agricultural lectures to remote rural students lacking broadband internet connectivity.\n\n2. National Digital Library of India (NDLI - Unified Academic Gateway):\n- Developed by IIT Kharagpur under the Ministry of Education, NDLI is a multilingual federated digital repository containing tens of millions of academic resources.\n- It aggregates digitized textbooks, ICAR annual reports, PhD theses, conference proceedings, and historical agrarian manuscripts. Students across peripheral colleges access premier global research literature through a single search portal.\n\n3. CeRA (Consortium for e-Resources in Agriculture - Research Access):\n- Established by ICAR in 2007 under NAIP, CeRA networks over 150 agricultural university libraries nationwide.\n- It provides free campus-wide electronic access to over 3,000 top-tier international peer-reviewed journals (Springer, Elsevier, Wiley, Nature), democratizing high-impact scientific literature for undergraduate and postgraduate scholars without expensive institutional subscription barriers.",
