      "modelAnswer": "e-Krishi Shiksha is an umbrella digital learning and education portal established by the Indian Council of Agricultural Research (ICAR) under the National Agricultural Higher Education Project (NAHEP).\n\nKey Components and Academic Utility:\n\n1. Curriculum-Aligned e-Courseware:\nHosts comprehensive, peer-reviewed digital textbooks and interactive multimedia modules mapped strictly to the national minimum syllabus formulated by the ICAR 5th Deans' Committee across B.Sc. (Hons.) Agriculture, Horticulture, Forestry, and Agricultural Engineering.\n\n2. Open-Access Study Notes and Question Banks:\nStudents can download chapter-wise PDF lecture notes, laboratory exercise manuals, and self-assessment quizzes prepared by senior SAU professors, ensuring academic uniformity across government and private agricultural colleges.\n\n3. Integration with Virtual Classrooms:\nProvides recorded video lectures, practical demonstration clips, and supplementary reading lists, serving as a reliable academic reference that eliminates the need to purchase expensive commercial textbooks.",
