      "questionText": "Formulate a strategic preparation plan for an agricultural graduate facing a behavioral and technical job interview at a leading drone-as-a-service (DaaS) AgriTech company.",
      "contextScenario": "Coaching a student finalist for an Operations Agronomist position at an agricultural drone enterprise.",
      "modelAnswer": "Securing a technical role in an AgriTech drone service company requires demonstrating both operational flight familiarity and agronomic domain competence.\n\n1. Technical Domain Mastery (The 'Hard Skills' Audit):\n- Regulatory Framework: Review DGCA Drone Rules 2021, Digital Sky airspace zones (Green/Yellow/Red), Remote Pilot Certificate (RPC) regulations, and CIB&RC approved agrochemical lists for drone spraying.\n- Spray Physics & Engineering: Master the mechanics of Controlled Droplet Application (CDA) rotary atomizers, droplet spectra (100-150 microns VMD), ultra-low volume application rates (8-15 L/ha), propeller downwash penetration, and drift thresholds (<10 km/h wind).\n- Multispectral Remote Sensing: Be prepared to explain NDVI/NDRE calculation, red edge shifts, downwelling light sensor calibration, and photogrammetry workflows in Pix4Dfields or Agisoft.\n\n2. Behavioral Preparation using STAR Framework:\nPrepare structured narratives addressing common behavioral questions:\n- Scenario: Managing operational conflict (e.g., a farmer demanding drone spraying during high winds).\n  * Situation: During a village demonstration, crosswinds reached 18 km/h.\n  * Task: The lead farmer insisted on immediate spraying to meet his irrigation schedule.\n  * Action: I politely paused operations, demonstrated the high off-target drift risk to his neighbor's sensitive crop using water-sensitive paper cards, and rescheduled flight for early next morning.\n  * Result: Achieved uniform deposition with zero drift damage, earning the farmer's long-term trust.\n\n3. The Reverse Interview (Asking High-Impact Questions):\nClose the interview by asking insightful questions that prove strategic thinking:\n- 'How is your flight operations team adapting to the battery degradation challenges in extreme northern Indian summer temperatures?'\n- 'What data pipeline are you using to translate raw drone multispectral orthomosaics into variable-rate prescription files compatible with older Indian tractor implements?'",
