      "questionText": "Construct a comprehensive guide for an agricultural graduate preparing for corporate AgriTech campus placements, detailing portfolio curation, mock case interviews, and LinkedIn recruiter outreach.",
      "contextScenario": "A comprehensive placement handbook for graduating agricultural science scholars.",
      "modelAnswer": "Securing high-tier placements in corporate AgriTech (precision farming, agri-fintech, supply chain logistics) requires agricultural graduates to position themselves as modern techno-commercial professionals.\n\n1. Digital Portfolio Curation (The Proof-of-Competence Engine):\n- Platform: Build a public digital portfolio hosted on Google Sites, Notion, or GitHub Pages.\n- Essential Project Showcases:\n  * Precision Agronomy Project: Highlighting a real QGIS spatial interpolation project with raw soil data, processed thematic fertility maps, and calculated fertilizer cost savings.\n  * Satellite Remote Sensing Workflow: A documented analysis tracking crop phenology and NDVI kinetics using Sentinel-2 imagery.\n  * RAWE / Rural Immersion Case Study: A documented field problem (e.g., managing fall armyworm outbreak) structured using the STAR method, with high-resolution field photos and farmer testimonials.\n  * Code Repositories: Link a clean GitHub repo containing documented R or Python scripts used for agricultural data analysis.\n\n2. Mastering the Technical Case Interview:\nAgriTech recruiters frequently present unstructured business-agronomy problems (e.g., 'A leading tomato processing company wants to contract 5,000 farmers in Karnataka. How would you design a digital monitoring and advisory system?'):\n- Step 1: Clarify Objectives & Constraints (Target crop, acreage, farmer smartphone penetration, pest risks).\n- Step 2: Structure the Operational Architecture (Sensing layer: Sentinel-2 + Plantix; Advisory layer: WhatsApp FPO channels; Procurement layer: digital weighment and QC assaying).\n- Step 3: Quantify Economic Impact & Unit Economics (Calculate operational cost per farmer vs reduced procurement spoilage).\n- Step 4: Propose Pilot Rollout & Risk Mitigation (Pilot with 250 farmers before full-scale deployment).\n\n3. Strategic LinkedIn Recruiter Outreach:\n- Profile Optimization: Headline stating technical specialization: 'B.Sc. (Hons.) Agriculture | Precision Farming, QGIS & Satellite Analytics | Graduate Agronomist'.\n- Content Creation: Share weekly technical takeaways from agricultural MOOCs, tagging relevant AgriTech leaders.\n- Proactive InMail Outreach: Send concise, personalized connection requests to founders and HR heads, linking directly to your digital portfolio and referencing their specific business challenges.",
